# A committed .semgrepignore replaces Semgrep's built-in list wholesale, which is the reason to commit one:
# the built-in list drops test/, tests/, build/, dist/ and vendor/, and python/tests/ starts a real ArangoDB
# and talks to it with real credentials.
# Guarded in both directions, because narrowing SAST scope is how a SAST gate dies without ever going red:
# semgrep-scan gets the paths that must not be excluded, disposition-check gets the allowlist of lines this
# file may contain. Adding a line here also takes a reviewed change to semgrepignore-allowed in config.yml.

.git/
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
build/
dist/
target/
vendor/

# The committed test-server key for the local ArangoDB fixture, a genuine finding excluded from SAST only:
# secret-scan still reports it every run, which is the tier whose job committed key material is.
# The real fix is generating this key at fixture start-up.
docker/server.pem
